</solution></exercise>
</example><exercise data-wait-for-event="eventShowMore1">
  <problem>
    <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
    <para>1. We cannot divide the number 100 by zero because dividing by zero is undefined. Instead, try dividing 100 by 10, then 1, then 0.1, then 0.01. What do you notice happens as you divide by smaller numbers? </para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>10, 100, 1000, 10,000. For example: The quotients are getting very large.</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<exercise data-wait-for-event="eventShowMore1">
  <problem>
    <para>2. Now try dividing the number -100 by 10, by 1, by 0.1, 0.01. What is the same and what is different when you compare to question 1?</para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>-10, -100, -1000, -10,000. For example: The absolute values of the quotients are the same, but the sign is
      opposite..</para>
  </solution></exercise>


